<newsitem itemid="349024" id="root" date="1997-01-31" xml:lang="en">
<title>SWITZERLAND: Julius Baer 1996 profit rises 16 pct.</title>
<headline>Julius Baer 1996 profit rises 16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to end December 31, 1996</p>
<p>				   (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net profit	     133.8	     vs 115.9</p>
<p> Return on equity (ROE),pct 11.0		vs 10.2</p>
<p> Div (bearer, Sfr)	    39		  vs 33</p>
<p> Div (regd, Sfr)		7.80		vs 6.60</p>
<p>NOTE - The Julius Baer Group said that thanks to the broad expansion of its business base, it expected another good result in 1997 providing that the international financial markets continue their positive trend.  </p>
<p>Earnings per bearer share</p>
<p> (Sfr)			    111.2	     vs 96.3</p>
<p> Cash flow per bearer, Sfr  137.8	     vs 124.0</p>
<p> Group gross profit	   196.6	     vs 175.4</p>
<p>Value adjustments,</p>
<p> provisions, losses	   11.5		vs 10.1</p>
<p> Operating income	     597.5	     vs 524.4</p>
<p> Operating expenses	   400.9	     vs 349.0</p>
<p> Net interest income	  112.3	     vs 115.7</p>
<p> Commissions, fees	    307.1	     vs 255.7</p>
<p> Trading results		148.3	     vs 130.2</p>
<p> of which securities	  76.9		vs 78.1</p>
<p> foreign exchange, notes    68.7		vs 49.1</p>
<p> Personnel expense	    251.3	     vs 219.4</p>
<p> Cash flow			162.4	     vs 146.2</p>
<p> Assets under management    63,600	    vs 49,400</p>
<p> of which investment funds  6,900	     vs 5,000</p>
<p> Total assets		   9,990.2	   vs 8,885.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Results are published according to International Accounting Standards (IAS) for the first time. Assets under management do not include global custody, which rose to 14.6 billion from 5.9 billion.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom 41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
